  "id": "F2",
  "title": "Per-attempt checkouts leak the base export after a crash",
  "file": "src/land/queue.ts",
  "A": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "The daemon restarts while a land is running its checks, which leaves that attempt's exported copy of the base commit on disk. Each attempt now uses a new directory name and the cleanup sweep does not match these copies, so they pile up in the work directory and are never deleted.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun $TMPDIR/f2.ts  (applies head's sweep filter from queue.ts:841-843 with id=7, attempts=3)",
    "output": "land-7 removed\nland-7-1 removed\nland-7-2 removed\nland-7-1-base kept\nland-7-2-base kept\nland-7-base kept\nland-7-3 kept\nland-70-1 kept"
   },
   "evidence": "At head, worktreePath = `land-${entry.id}-${entry.attempts}` (queue.ts:827) and checks() exports to `${cwd}-base` (queue.ts:436). On a normal exit the `finally` deletes it, but a crash skips that. The sweep at queue.ts:841-843 keeps any name whose suffix after `land-<id>-` is not all digits, so `land-<id>-<n>-base` and the legacy `land-<id>-base` survive. At base, worktreePath was the fixed `land-<id>`, so the next attempt's `rmSync(base)` deleted a crashed attempt's export. Nothing in gc.ts cleans `land-*` directories."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "The daemon crashes while running landing checks, leaving a copy of the base source on disk. After restart, the next attempt leaves that abandoned copy behind, so crashes can accumulate unused source directories.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun test \"${TMPDIR%/}/limitless-adjudication.FLud9G/claims.test.ts\"",
    "output": "F2 {\"attempt\":2,\"oldWorktreeExists\":false,\"legacyWorktreeExists\":false,\"oldBaseExists\":true,\"legacyBaseExists\":true,\"currentBase\":\"land-1-2-base\"}\n2 pass\n0 fail"
   },
   "evidence": "The temporary test seeded abandoned directories and invoked HEAD's checkout method after a real Store reclaim, mocking only Git worktree operations. The actual sweep removed the older checkout directories but retained both base exports. HEAD changes worktreePath to `land-${entry.id}-${entry.attempts}` (826\u2013827), while checks still uses `const base = `${cwd}-base`` and removes only that path (436\u2013438,507\u2013508). The sweep accepts only the legacy checkout name or an entirely numeric attempt suffix (841\u2013845), excluding both `land-1-1-base` and `land-1-base`. At base, every attempt reused `land-${entry.id}`, so the next checks invocation removed the previous export using its unchanged path. The demonstrated consequence is abandoned disk usage, requiring a crash during checks."
  }
